I agree the {abu boi reroi broda} thing is annoying, but... it's just a ter=
minator. There are a lot of places in Lojban where you have to remember to =
un-elide terminators in certain situations. I'm not sure this one is annoyi=
ng _enough_ to change the grammar.

FWIW, la zipcpi's mid-way proposal would be to do the separation for "bare"=
 lerfu/number strings (btw I guess we have to change the definition of {ler=
fu} if this goes through) but leave mex alone, so {cy ci .ibu} would be two=
 sumti while {li cy ci .ibu} would be one, in other words {li} would take a=
ny number of number-strings and/or lerfu-strings, similar to how {la} takes=
 any number of cmevla. It would avoid any changes to mex and preserve thing=
s like that really nice date format proposal. On the other hand it reduces =
consistency a tiny bit.

mu'o mi'e durkavore

